docs/DECISIONS.md-55-Reason: The schema intentionally grants authenticated admins update rights only to review fields and status metadata. A real Supabase smoke test caught a 403 when application code tried to patch `submission_id`, proving the column-scoped grant is working and should remain part of the safety model.
docs/DECISIONS.md-56-
docs/DECISIONS.md-57-## 2026-10-31: Museum Acts 03 and 04 use placeholders until a public-safe archive view exists
docs/DECISIONS.md-58-
docs/DECISIONS.md:59:Decision: The MOFUNDO museum experience (Acts 03 "People × Places × Sound" and 04 "The Story So Far") renders clearly marked placeholder data from a typed adapter. No real people, encounters, or counters are shown until a public-safe view or API exists.
docs/DECISIONS.md-60-
docs/DECISIONS.md-61-Reason: The archive tables are default-deny for `anon` under RLS. Exposing approved data publicly requires a Tier 3 review of grants, RLS, and contributor privacy. Placeholders keep the museum buildable without weakening access controls or inventing personal history.
docs/DECISIONS.md-62-
docs/DECISIONS.md-63-## 2026-10-31: Museum transition targets the real interview start
--
docs/DECISIONS.md-71-Decision: Museum audio is configured in `src/lib/museumAudioConfig.ts` with a placeholder path (`/media/museum-ambient.mp3`). No external track is downloaded or committed. Audio is off by default, never autoplays, and the museum must work with the file absent.
docs/DECISIONS.md-72-
docs/DECISIONS.md-73-Reason: Yeriel will replace the placeholder with his own MOFUNDO music. Bundling a third-party track would need licensing review and would conflict with that plan.
docs/DECISIONS.md-74-
docs/DECISIONS.md:75:## 2026-10-31: Museum is one cinematic sequence of four scenes, not an interactive exhibit
docs/DECISIONS.md-76-
docs/DECISIONS.md:77:Decision: The museum is a guided, scroll-driven sequence with four scenes: 01 YERIEL, 02 MOFUNDO, 03 HOW DO YOU REMEMBER HIM?, 04 JOIN THE STORY. The only controls are ENTER, the persistent sound toggle, and the final TELL ME HOW WE MET → link into `/remember/write`. Clickable constellation nodes, museum labels, act navigation, and the separate Story So Far scene are removed. Archive counters move into Scene 04.
docs/DECISIONS.md-78-
docs/DECISIONS.md-79-Reason: The goal is a single cinematic journey that ends by inviting contribution. Interactive exploration would split attention from the story and weaken the final call to action.
docs/DECISIONS.md-80-
docs/DECISIONS.md-81-## 2026-10-31: Museum uses labeled placeholder images
--
