docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md-535-## 20. Archive Data
docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md-536-
docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md:537:- **Typed adapter** `MuseumArchiveAdapter` returns a `MuseumDataset`. Every entity carries `source: 'placeholder' | 'archive'`. Every counter carries `status: 'placeholder' | 'live' | 'pending'`.
docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md:538:- **Placeholder adapter is the only implementation** until a public-safe view is approved (D3). Placeholder counter values are returned with `status: 'placeholder'` and rendered with the `PLACEHOLDER VALUES` tag.
docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md:539:- **Public-safe view or endpoint** (later, Tier 3 review): returns only approved, public-safe records. No contributor contact, no private notes, no original-submission JSON, no review fields. Names only when `attributionPreference` allows. Anonymous stays anonymous. Counts are aggregates, not per-person.
docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md-540-- **Client never queries private tables.** Data reaches the sequence through a server route or a reviewed view.
docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md-541-- **Layers stay separate** (per `docs/HISTORICAL_INTEGRITY.md`): contributor memory, Yeriel's material, AI observation, confirmed evidence, and story drafts are never merged on the stage. Only approved contributor memories and approved Yeriel-authored material appear.
docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md-542-- **AI never writes museum copy as fact.** AI prose is never shown as a memory.
docs/MOFUNDO_MUSEUM_DESIGN_BIBLE.md:543:- The existing `attributionPreference` field in `src/lib/types.ts` is the attribution control the museum must honor.
