155-**Rules**
156-- No roll. Pitch and yaw ≤ 3°, and only in Scene 03 for depth feel.
157:- Scroll velocity is clamped. A fast flick cannot skip a scene's key moment: the camera eases to the scene's key frame.
158-- The camera never moves on pointer input. No parallax on desktop or mobile.
159-- Reduced motion: no camera travel at all. Scenes transition by crossfade and the static composition for each scene is used instead.
--
166-- **Durations:** element enter 700–900ms; scene transform 1.6–2.4s, driven by scroll (not time).
167-- **Scroll is the clock.** Animations are tied to scroll progress. Time-based animation is used only for the loader, counters, and the final hand-off.
168:- **Permanent motion:** dust in light (desktop only) and a slow grain shift. Both stop under reduced motion.
169-- **Stillness is a scene element.** Scene 04's final moments are a hold with nearly no motion.
170-
--
190-
191-- Particles are **dust in light**. They appear only in the beam over the current focal subject. They do not represent people or data.
192:- Counts: desktop ≤ 300; mobile ≤ 40; low-power and reduced motion: 0.
193-- Drift ≤ 4px/s. No pointer reactions.
194-- Particles fade in Scene 04 and vanish at the final message.
--
