436:## 16. Accessibility
437-
438-- **Structure:** one `<main>`, one `<h1>` ("Yeriel" for Scene 01 text), and `<h2>`s for each scene's heading, visually small or hidden where the visual is the heading.
439-- **Text version:** the whole sequence is also available as ordered text in the DOM, in scene order (a visually hidden block, or a "Read as text" view). Screen-reader users hear the same four scenes, the counters with their labels and placeholder/pending status, and the CTA. This is the accessible equivalent of the scroll and is not optional.
440:- **Focus:** 2px `--purple` ring with 2px offset. Visible on the ENTER control, the sound control, the leave link, the skip link, and the CTA.
441-- **Keyboard:** Tab reaches the controls in visual order. Space, Page Down and arrow keys scroll the sequence normally.
442-- **Live regions:** none for scroll-driven changes. Scene headings are not announced as they appear. No aria-live spam.
--
